ght="72" rx="3" width="6" x="34" y="460"></rect><text class="lane-label" x="56" y="491">EXECUTION</text><text class="legend" x="56" y="512">What paths, waits and rework actually occurred?</text><g transform="translate(390 477)"><rect class="lane-node execution" height="38" rx="9" width="100"></rect><text class="node-title" x="50" y="24">Decision</text></g><g transform="translate(520 477)"><rect class="lane-node execution" height="38" rx="9" width="102"></rect><text class="node-title" x="51" y="24">Approval</text></g><g transform="translate(652 477)"><rect class="lane-node execution" height="38" rx="9" width="140"></rect><text class="node-title" x="70" y="24">Manual Review</text></g><g transform="translate(814 477)"><rect class="lane-node execution" height="38" rx="9" width="112"></rect><text class="node-title" x="56" y="24">Exception</text></g><text class="insight insight-teal" x="1090" y="500">18% manual review</text><rect class="lane-bg-systems" height="72" rx="14" width="1312" x="34" y="546"></rect><rect class="lane-accent-systems" height="72" rx="3" width="6" x="34" y="546"></rect><text class="lane-label" x="56" y="577">SYSTEMS</text><text class="legend" x="56" y="598">Which platforms, services and APIs participated?</text><g transform="translate(390 563)"><rect class="lane-node system" height="38" rx="9" width="82"></rect><text class="node-title" x="41" y="24">API</text></g><g transform="translate(500 563)"><rect class="lane-node system" height="38" rx="9" width="118"></rect><text class="node-title" x="59" y="24">Application</text></g><g transform="translate(646 563)"><rect class="lane-node system" height="38" rx="9" width="92"></rect><text class="node-title" x="46" y="24">Queue</text></g><g transform="translate(766 563)"><rect class="lane-node system" height="38" rx="9" width="96"></rect><text class="node-title" x="48" y="24">Service</text></g><text class="insight insight-blue" x="1090" y="586">4 systems · 1 retry path</text><rect class="lane-bg-tech" height="72" rx="14" width="1312" x="34" y="632"></rect><rect class="lane-accent-tech" height="72" rx="3" width="6" x="34" y="632"></rect><text class="lane-label" x="56" y="663">TECHNOLOGY</text><text class="legend" x="56" y="684">What technology resources were used?</text><g transform="translate(390 649)"><rect class="lane-node tech" height="38" rx="9" width="104"></rect><text class="node-title" x="52" y="24">Cloud Job</text></g><g transform="translate(524 649)"><rect class="lane-node tech" height="38" rx="9" width="108"></rect><text class="node-title" x="54" y="24">Database</text></g><text class="insight insight-copper" x="1090" y="672">Egress 4% · Compute 11%</text><line class="cross" x1="458" x2="440" y1="429" y2="477"></line><line class="cross" x1="440" x2="430" y1="515" y2="563"></line><line class="cross" x1="430" x2="440" y1="601" y2="649"></line><line class="cross" x1="651" x2="572" y1="429" y2="477"></line><line class="cross" x1="572" x2="559" y1="515" y2="563"></line><line class="cross" x1="559" x2="578" y1="601" y2="649"></line></svg></div></section></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="section-transition"></div><div class="page-section" id="ont-s3"><section class="section"><div class="layout"><div class="left"><div class="kicker">FROM RELATIONSHIPS TO DECISIONS</div><h1>RE-ViVE Gives the CIO Organization a New View of the Enterprise.</h1><div class="intro">By connecting business execution to the systems and technology that support it, RE-ViVE helps CIO teams answer practical questions about cost, performance, dependencies, risk and modernization.</div></div><div class="right"><div class="right-label">QUESTIONS RE-ViVE HELPS ANSWER</div><div class="grid"><article class="card"><div class="tag">RATIONALIZATION</div><div class="icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#5A47B8" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 7h14M8 12h8M6 17h12"></path></svg></div><h2>Technology Overlap</h2><p>Which platforms provide overlapping execution capabilities across business units?</p></article><article class="card"><div class="tag">OPERATIONS</div><div class="icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#5A47B8" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 8l3 3 6-6"></path><path d="M5 16h14"></path></svg></div><h2>Workflow Dependency</h2><p>Which systems and jobs are critical to an end-to-end business workflow?</p></article><article class="card"><div class="tag">FINOPS</div><div class="icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#5A47B8" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 4v16M9 7.5c0-1.5 1.2-2.5 3-2.5s3 1 3 2.5-1.3 2.2-3 2.5-3 .9-3 2.5 1.2 2.5 3 2.5 3-1 3-2.5"></path></svg></div><h2>Cost by Outcome</h2><p>Where is technology cost accumulating across specific execution paths?</p></article><article class="card"><div class="tag">ARCHITECTURE</div><div class="icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#5A47B8" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><rect height="10" rx="1.5" width="10" x="5" y="7"></rect><rect height="10" rx="1.5" width="10" x="9" y="3"></rect></svg></div><h2>Redundancy</h2><p>Where do duplicate jobs, data movements, or shadow platforms exist?</p></article><article class="card"><div class="tag">RELIABILITY</div><div class="icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#5A47B8" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M13 2L6 13h5l-1 9 7-12h-5l1-8z"></path></svg></div><h2>Performance</h2><p>Which jobs or runtime dependencies are slowing down the workflow?</p></article><article class="card"><div class="tag">EFFICIENCY</div><div class="icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#5A47B8" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 16l4-5 3 3 5-7"></path><path d="M5 19h14"></path></svg></div><h2>Utilization</h2><p>Which technology is heavily used, lightly used, or easily avoidable?</p></article><article class="card"><div class="tag">RISK &amp; CHANGE</div><div class="icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#5A47B8" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"></circle><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"></circle></svg></div><h2>Change Impact</h2><p>What business execution could be disrupted by an upcoming technology change?</p></article><article class="card"><div class="tag">MODERNIZATION</div><div class="icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#5A47B8" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M7 5l5 7-5 7M13 5l4 7-4 7"></path></svg></div><h2>Consolidation</h2><p>Where is there empirical evidence to retire, consolidate, or modernize platforms?</p></article></div></div></div></section></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="section-transition"></div><div class="page-section" id="ont-s4"><section class="section"><div class="kicker">AI + EXECUTION CONTEXT</div><h1>AI Can Discover the Enterprise. Execution Shows How It Actually Runs.</h1><div class="lead">AI can accelerate the discovery of relationships across enterprise information. RE-ViVE adds the execution dimension—showing how those relationships are actually used across real transactions, paths, variants and outcomes.</div><div class="row"><div class="copy"><div class="eyebrow">AI-ASSISTED DISCOVERY</div><h2>Discover the relationships.</h2><p>AI can rapidly explore documents, code, schemas, APIs, metadata and logs to identify and connect likely relationships across the enterprise.</p><div class="mini">A faster starting point for building enterprise context.</div></div><div class="visual ai"><img alt="AI-assisted discovery of enterprise relationships" decoding="async" height="569" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 980px) 92vw, 66vw" src="/images/ontology/ontology-ai-assisted-discovery-1600.webp" srcset="/images/ontology/ontology-ai-assisted-discovery-800.webp 800w, /images/ontology/ontology-ai-assisted-discovery-1600.webp 1600w" width="1600"/></div></div><div class="bridge"><div class="small">THE EXECUTION DIMENSION</div><h3>Discovery establishes relationships. RE-ViVE adds the execution reality.</h3><p>Knowing what is connected does not show how work actually moves through those connections—or how often different paths, retries, approvals and exceptions occur.</p></div><div class="row revive-row"><div class="copy"><div class="eyebrow">RE-ViVE EXECUTION EVIDENCE</div><h2>See how the relationships are actually used.</h2><p>RE-ViVE organizes transaction-level execution into paths, variants and observed patterns—connecting volume, timing, exceptions and outcomes to the systems and technology involved.</p><div class="mini">Not just the workflow definition. The evidence of how work actually executed.</div></div><div class="visual revive"><img alt="RE-ViVE observed execution paths and variants" decoding="async" height="800" loading="lazy" sizes="(max-width: 980px) 92vw, 66vw" src="/images/ontology/ontology-revive-execution-evidence-1600.webp" srcset="/images/ontology/ontology-revive-execution-evidence-800.webp 800w, /images/ontology/ontology-revive-execution-evidence-1600.webp 1600w" width="1600"/></div></div><div class="conclusion"><h3>Discovery + execution creates richer enterprise context.</h3><p>Together, AI-assisted discovery and observed execution can strengthen enterprise ontology and give technology leaders better context for analysis and decisions.</p></div></section></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="section-transition"></div><div class="page-section" id="ont-s5"><section class="section"><div class="kicker">PUTTING IT TO WORK</div><h1>Examples Across the Enterprise.</h1><div class="intro">Whether the workflow is customer-facing, technology-driven or financial, RE-ViVE connects the business outcome to how work executes, the systems involved and the technology underneath.</div><div class="examples"><article class="example" id="capital-markets-example"><div class="example-head"><div class="num">01</div><div class="title-wrap"><h2>Capital Markets</h2><div class="sub">Trade Processing &amp; Settlement</div></div><div class="lenses"><div class="lens business"><div class="lens-label"><span class="lens-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#5A47B8" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 18V9h5v9M14 18V5h5v13M3 20h18"></path></svg></span>BUSINESS</div><p>Institutional trade → settlement outcome</p></div><div class="lens execution"><div class="lens-label"><span class="lens-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#2D6A68" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="5" cy="12" r="2"></circle><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="2"></circle><circle cx="19" cy="12" r="2"></circle><path d="M7 11l3-3M14 8l3 3M7 13h10"></path></svg></span>EXECUTION</div><p>Trade Capture → Validation → Allocation → Exception / Repair → Settlement</p></div><div class="lens systems"><div class="lens-label"><span class="lens-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#407DA8" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><rect height="6" rx="1.5" width="16" x="4" y="5"></rect><rect height="6" rx="1.5" width="16" x="4" y="13"></rect><path d="M8 8h.01M8 16h.01"></path></svg></span>SYSTEMS</div><p>Order Management → Trade Processing → Risk / Compliance → Settlement Platform → Custodian</p></div><div class="lens technology"><div class="lens-label"><span class="lens-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#A94708" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M8 4h8v5H8zM5 15h5v5H5zM14 15h5v5h-5zM12 9v3M7.5 15v-3H16.5v3"></path></svg></span>TECHNOLOGY</div><p>APIs · message queues · batch jobs · databases · cloud / compute dependencies</p></div></div></div><div class="insight"><strong>What becomes visible:</strong> where exceptions, manual repairs, dependencies and technology behavior affect settlement.</div><a class="paper-link" href="/article-capital-markets-ontology-accelerator">See the Capital Markets example →</a></article><article class="example"><div class="example-head"><div class="num">02</div><div class="title-wrap"><h2>Application Delivery</h2><div class="sub">From Business Change to Production</div></div><div class="lenses"><div class="lens business"><div class="lens-label"><span class="lens-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#5A47B8" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 18V9h5v9M14 18V5h5v13M3 20h18"></path></svg></span>BUSINESS</div><p>Requested capability → production release</p></div><div class="lens execution"><div class="lens-label"><span class="lens-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#2D6A68" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="5" cy="12" r="2"></circle><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="2"></circle><circle cx="19" cy="12" r="2"></circle><path d="M7 11l3-3M14 8l3 3M7 13h10"></path></svg></span>EXECUTION</div><p>Requirement → Development → Build → Test → Approval → Deployment → Production</p></div><div class="lens systems"><div class="lens-label"><span class="lens-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#407DA8" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><rect height="6" rx="1.5" width="16" x="4" y="5"></rect><rect height="6" rx="1.5" width="16" x="4" y="13"></rect><path d="M8 8h.01M8 16h.01"></path></svg></span>SYSTEMS</div><p>Work Management → Source Control → CI/CD → Test Platform → Change Management → Production</p></div><div class="lens technology"><div class="lens-label"><span class="lens-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#A94708" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M8 4h8v5H8zM5 15h5v5H5zM14 15h5v5h-5zM12 9v3M7.5 15v-3H16.5v3"></path></svg></span>TECHNOLOGY</div><p>Build compute · pipeline runtime · deployment infrastructure · cloud resources · environment utilization</p></div></div></div><div class="insight"><strong>What becomes visible:</strong> where delivery slows, which systems and technology contribute, and where repeated work or dependencies accumulate.</div></article><article class="example"><div class="example-head"><div class="num">03</div><div class="title-wrap"><h2>Order to Cash Reporting</h2><div class="sub">From Operational Activity to Management View</div></div><div class="lenses"><div class="lens business"><div class="lens-label"><span class="lens-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#5A47B8" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 18V9h5v9M14 18V5h5v13M3 20h18"></path></svg></span>BUSINESS</div><p>Order to cash performance → management reporting</p></div><div class="lens execution"><div class="lens-label"><span class="lens-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#2D6A68" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="5" cy="12" r="2"></circle><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="2"></circle><circle cx="19" cy="12" r="2"></circle><path d="M7 11l3-3M14 8l3 3M7 13h10"></path></svg></span>EXECUTION</div><p>Order Activity → Data Extraction → Transformation → Aggregation → Report Refresh → Consumption</p></div><div class="lens systems"><div class="lens-label"><span class="lens-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#407DA8" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><rect height="6" rx="1.5" width="16" x="4" y="5"></rect><rect height="6" rx="1.5" width="16" x="4" y="13"></rect><path d="M8 8h.01M8 16h.01"></path></svg></span>SYSTEMS</div><p>SAP / CRM → Data Lake → Databricks / ETL → Snowflake → Power BI</p></div><div class="lens technology"><div class="lens-label"><span class="lens-icon"><svg fill="none" stroke="#A94708" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M8 4h8v5H8zM5 15h5v5H5zM14 15h5v5h-5zM12 9v3M7.5 15v-3H16.5v3"></path></svg></span>TECHNOLOGY</div><p>Scheduled jobs · data movement · compute · storage · refresh frequency · runtime dependencies</p></div></div></div><div class="insight"><strong>What becomes visible:</strong> which jobs and platforms support each reporting outcome, where capabilities overlap, and where technology cost and complexity accumulate.</div></article></div><div class="more"><div class="more-label">AND MANY MORE</div><p>The same approach can be applied to <strong>health insurance claims</strong>,<strong>supply chain execution</strong>, <strong>mortgage processing</strong>,<strong>commercial loan approval</strong>, customer onboarding, payments, service operations and other workflows where business outcomes depend on a connected chain of execution, systems and technology.</p></div></section></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="section-transition"></div><div class="page-section" id="ont-s6"><section class="cta"><div class="cta-inner"><div class="kicker">START WITH ONE WORKFLOW</div><h1>Don't Wait for the Entire Enterprise Ontology.</h1><div class="lead">Start with a business workflow where execution evidence already exists. RE-ViVE can establish a practical foundation of observed relationships and execution context—then expand from there.</div><button class="cta-button" id="openDrawer"><a href="mailto:connect@revivetoday.com" style="text-decoration: none !important;"> Explore an Execution Context Pilot </a></button></div></section><div class="overlay" id="overlay"></div><aside aria-hidden="true" class="drawer" id="drawer"><div class="drawer-inner"><div class="drawer-head"><div><div class="drawer-kicker">EXECUTION CONTEXT PILOT</div><h2>Start with one workflow. Build from evidence.</h2></div><button aria-label="Close panel" class="close" id="closeDrawer">×</button></div><div class="drawer-intro">Begin with a defined workflow and historical execution data. RE-ViVE establishes connected execution context that can support and accelerate broader ontology initiatives.</div><div class="pilot-table"><div class="row header"><div class="cell">#</div><div class="cell">PHASE</div><div class="cell">WHAT HAPPENS</div><div class="cell who">WHO</div></div><div class="row"><div class="cell step">01</div><div class="cell phase">Define</div><div class="cell">Select one workflow, historical period and the questions to explore.</div><div class="cell who"><span class="pill both">Client + RE-ViVE</span></div></div><div class="row"><div class="cell step">02</div><div class="cell phase">Connect</div><div class="cell">Client provides approved read-only access; RE-ViVE extracts the required execution data.</div><div class="cell who"><span class="pill both">Client + RE-ViVE</span></div></div><div class="row"><div class="cell step">03</div><div class="cell phase">Build</div><div class="cell">RE-ViVE correlates the evidence and connects business, execution, systems and technology.</div><div class="cell who"><span class="pill revive">RE-ViVE</span></div></div><div class="row"><div class="cell step">04</div><div class="cell phase">Refine</div><div class="cell">Review the first connected view together and add any important missing context.</div><div class="cell who"><span class="pill both">Client + RE-ViVE</span></div></div><div class="row"><div class="cell step">05</div><div class="cell phase">Present</div><div class="cell">RE-ViVE presents the execution paths, relationships, dependencies and key findings.</div><div class="cell who"><span class="pill revive">RE-ViVE</span></div></div></div><div class="highlight"><strong>First meaningful views can emerge in days.</strong><span>Start with historical data. No need to wait for an enterprise-wide initiative.</span></div><div class="production"><div class="label">FROM PILOT TO PRODUCTION</div><h3>Keep the execution context current.</h3><p>If the pilot proves valuable, move to differential data loads at an agreed frequency—or near-real-time/live ingestion where appropriate.</p><div class="progression"><span>Historical Data</span><b>→</b><span>Pilot</span><b>→</b><span>Validated Context</span><b>→</b><span>Production</span><b>→</b><span>Continuous Updates</span></div></div><div class="deploy"><div class="label">RUN IT WHERE YOU NEED IT</div><div class="deploy-title">Your environment. Your controls.</div><div class="deploy-pills"><span>On-Premises</span><span>Your Cloud</span><span>Private Cloud / SaaS</span></div><div class="assurance">Read-only source access · No production application changes</div></div><button class="drawer-action">Request a Discussion</button></div></aside></div></div></main>
